{
  "out": "/tmp/photonz-playtest/flip-by-dragging-a-handle-walk",
  "seed": "A side handle dragged past the side opposite flips the layer and keeps going, as in Photoshop and Figma, at Next defaults with no flag changed (the user, 2026-10-20: dragging to reverse it did not work, the box stopped at nothing). A picture half dark and half light, 900 by 700, is dropped on a 2000 by 1400 canvas at 550, 350. Its right handle is dragged 200 past its left edge: the picture is 200 wide from 350 to 550, flipped left to right. Its bottom handle is dragged 100 above its top: 100 tall from 250 to 350, flipped top to bottom as well. One undo puts back only the second drag. Last, typed words have their right side dragged past their left and read mirrored.",
